  "steps": [
    "Cut the two side panels with a 10 in circle cut 6 in up from the bottom and 2 in from the front.",
    "Cut the top crosspiece and the bottom shelf board, then screw the sides to the crosspiece.",
    "Screw the top at the back so the bowls sit on the closed surface and the front stays open.",
    "Drill a pilot hole and screw a cleat under the shelf to stop the sides bowing.",
    "Sand and apply a coat of exterior sealer so spill-proof bowls do not stain it."
